  "summary": "The paper introduces QNUTE, a gate-based quantum algorithm for simulating arbitrary non-Hermitian dynamics, and applies it to Black-Scholes option pricing. It reports noiseless simulations on 2- to 6-qubit instances with exact-case fidelities reaching 1.0 and inexact-case fidelities dropping substantially when the unitary domain is restricted (e.g., around 0.13–0.71 for some 5–6 qubit settings).",
